#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:4
msgid "Syncthing Relay Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:7
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:11
msgid ""
"strelaysrv [-debug] [-ext-address=<address>] [-global-rate=<bytes/s>] [-"
"keys=<dir>] [-listen=<listen addr>]\n"
"           [-message-timeout=<duration>] [-nat] [-nat-lease=<duration>] [-"
"nat-renewal=<duration>]\n"
"           [-nat-timeout=<duration>] [-network-timeout=<duration>] [-per-"
"session-rate=<bytes/s>]\n"
"           [-ping-interval=<duration>] [-pools=<pool addresses>] [-pprof] [-"
"protocol=<string>]\n"
"           [-provided-by=<string>] [-status-srv=<listen addr>] [-"
"token=<string>] [-version]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:18
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:20
msgid ""
"Syncthing relies on a network of community-contributed relay servers. Anyone "
"can run a relay server, and it will automatically join the relay pool and be "
"available to Syncthing users. The current list of relays can be found at "
"https://relays.syncthing.net/."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:26
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:30
msgid "Enable debug output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:34
msgid ""
"An optional address to advertising as being available on. Allows listening "
"on an unprivileged port with port forwarding from e.g. 443, and be connected "
"to on port 443."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:40
msgid "Global rate limit, in bytes/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:44
msgid "Directory where cert.pem and key.pem is stored (default \".\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:48
msgid "Protocol listen address (default \":22067\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:52
msgid ""
"Maximum amount of time we wait for relevant messages to arrive (default "
"1m0s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:56
msgid "Use UPnP/NAT-PMP to acquire external port mapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:60
msgid "NAT lease length in minutes (default 60)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:64
msgid "NAT renewal frequency in minutes (default 30)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:68
msgid "NAT discovery timeout in seconds (default 10)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:72
msgid ""
"Timeout for network operations between the client and the relay. If no data "
"is received between the client and the relay in this period of time, the "
"connection is terminated. Furthermore, if no data is sent between either "
"clients being relayed within this period of time, the session is also "
"terminated. (default 2m0s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:80
msgid "Per session rate limit, in bytes/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:84
msgid "How often pings are sent (default 1m0s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:88
msgid ""
"Comma separated list of relay pool addresses to join (default \"https://"
"relays.syncthing.net/endpoint\"). Blank to disable announcement to a pool, "
"thereby remaining a private relay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:94
msgid "Enable the built in profiling on the status server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:98
msgid ""
"Protocol used for listening. 'tcp' for IPv4 and IPv6, 'tcp4' for IPv4, "
"'tcp6' for IPv6 (default \"tcp\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:102
msgid "An optional description about who provides the relay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:106
msgid ""
"Listen address for status service (blank to disable) (default \":22070\"). "
"Status service is used by the relay pool server UI for displaying stats "
"(data transferred, number of clients, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:111
msgid ""
"Token to restrict access to the relay (optional). Disables joining any pools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:115
msgid "Show version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:118
msgid "Installing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:120
msgid ""
"Go to `releases <https://github.com/syncthing/relaysrv/releases>`__ and "
"download the file appropriate for your operating system. Unpacking it will "
"yield a binary called ``strelaysrv`` (or ``strelaysrv.exe`` on Windows). "
"Start this in whatever way you are most comfortable with; double clicking "
"should work in any graphical environment. At first start, strelaysrv will "
"generate certificate files and database in the current directory unless "
"given flags to the contrary. It will also join the default pools of relays, "
"which means that it is publicly visible and any client can connect to it. "
"The startup message prints instructions on how to change this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:130
msgid ""
"The relay server can also be obtained through apt, the Debian/Ubuntu package "
"manager. Recent releases can be found at syncthing's `apt repository "
"<https://apt.syncthing.net/>`_. The name of the package is syncthing-"
"relaysrv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:136
msgid "Setting Up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:138
msgid ""
"Primarily, you need to decide on a directory to store the TLS key and "
"certificate and a listen port. The default listen port of 22067 works, but "
"for optimal compatibility a well known port for encrypted traffic such as "
"443 is recommended. This may require additional setup to work without "
"running as root or a privileged user, see `Running on port 443 as an "
"unprivileged user`_ below. In principle something similar to this should "
"work on a Linux/Unix system::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:146
msgid ""
"$ sudo useradd strelaysrv\n"
"$ sudo mkdir /etc/strelaysrv\n"
"$ sudo chown strelaysrv /etc/strelaysrv\n"
"$ sudo -u strelaysrv /usr/local/bin/strelaysrv -keys /etc/strelaysrv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:151
msgid ""
"This creates a user ``strelaysrv`` and a directory ``/etc/strelaysrv`` to "
"store the keys. The keys are generated on first startup. The relay will join "
"the global relay pool, unless a ``-pools=\"\"`` argument is given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:155
msgid ""
"To make the relay server start automatically at boot, use the recommended "
"procedure for your operating system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:159
msgid "Client configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:161
msgid ""
"Syncthing can be configured to use specific relay servers (exclusively of "
"the public pool) by adding the required servers to the Sync Protocol Listen "
"Address field, under Actions and Settings. The format is as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:163
msgid "relay://<host name|IP>[:port]/?id=<relay device ID>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:165
msgid "For example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:167
msgid ""
"relay://private-relay-1.example.com:443/?id=ITZRNXE-YNROGBZ-HXTH5P7-VK5NYE5-"
"QHRQGE2-7JQ6VNJ-KZUEDIU-5PPR5AM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:169
msgid "The relay's device ID is output on start-up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:172
msgid "Running on port 443 as an unprivileged user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:174
msgid ""
"It is recommended that you run the relay on port 443 (or another port which "
"is commonly allowed through corporate firewalls), in order to maximise the "
"chances that people are able to connect. However, binding to ports below "
"1024 requires root privileges, and running a relay as root is not "
"recommended. Thankfully there are a couple of approaches available to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:180
msgid ""
"One option is to run the relay on port 22067, and use an ``iptables`` rule "
"to forward traffic from port 443 to port 22067, for example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:183
msgid ""
"iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p tcp --dport 443 -j REDIRECT --to-port 22067"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:185
msgid ""
"Or, if you're using ``ufw``, add the following to ``/etc/ufw/before.rules``::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:187
msgid ""
"*nat\n"
":PREROUTING ACCEPT [0:0]\n"
":POSTROUTING ACCEPT [0:0]\n"
"\n"
"-A PREROUTING -p tcp --dport 443 -j REDIRECT --to-port 22067\n"
"\n"
"COMMIT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:195
msgid ""
"You will need to start ``strelaysrv`` with ``-ext-address \":443\"``. This "
"tells ``strelaysrv`` that it can be contacted on port 443, even though it is "
"listening on port 22067. You will also need to let both port 443 and 22067 "
"through your firewall."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:200
msgid ""
"Another option is `described here <https://wiki.apache.org/httpd/"
"NonRootPortBinding>`__, although your mileage may vary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:204
msgid "Firewall Considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:206
msgid ""
"The relay server listens on two ports by default.  One for data connections "
"and the other for providing public statistics at https://relays.syncthing."
"net/.  The firewall, such as ``iptables``, must permit incoming TCP "
"connections to the following ports:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:210
msgid ""
"Data port:  ``22067/tcp`` overridden with ``-listen`` and advertised with ``-"
"ext-address``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:211
msgid "Status port: ``22070/tcp`` overridden with ``-status-srv``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:213
msgid "Runtime ``iptables`` rules to allow access to the default ports::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:215
msgid ""
"iptables -I INPUT -p tcp --dport 22067 -j ACCEPT\n"
"iptables -I INPUT -p tcp --dport 22070 -j ACCEPT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:218
msgid ""
"Please consult Linux distribution documentation to persist firewall rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:221
msgid "Access control for private relays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:225
msgid ""
"Private relays can be configured to only accept connections from peers in "
"possession of a shared secret. To configure this use the ``-token`` option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:228
msgid "$ strelaysrv -token=mySecretToken"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:230
msgid ""
"Then configure your Syncthing devices to send the token when joining the "
"relay::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/strelaysrv.rst:232
msgid "relay://<host name|IP>[:port]/?id=<relay device ID>&token=mySecretToken"
msgstr ""

